{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets","id":433128,"title":"Siskur-Dah - 2ed Sacred Hunt and it's secrets","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-03-08T14:40:18-07:00","id":433128,"title":"Siskur-Dah - 2ed Sacred Hunt and it's secrets","content":"So in 2ed, <i>Siskur-Dah</i> is 2nd dot Rite that almost all Uratha do - because &quot;Wolf Must Hunt&quot;. But there are some problems with that. Do not get me wrong, I really love this concept - but some things just arise. Like...<br /> <br /> <b>Should not be the &quot;free&quot; Rite?</b> Every werewolf on the Earth must do this at least once per month. Their Auspices and Tribes culture is totally based on this Sacred Hunt. New corebook sounds like every Uratha is calling the Hunt on the whims of his Blood. <b>So <i>wh</i>y does every character need to have 2 dots in Rites, if it's so crucial and inner to werewolf state to use for them?</b> It's illogical, in-setting and outside of it. Should not just Uratha get ability to invoke Scared Hunt, just like they Reaching to the Shadow Realm or shapeshift - things that are inner abilites of races, but still the need to learn? If the Hunt is &quot;in their Blood&quot;, why do all players should pay for it with extra Experience? Or at least why it's not 1 dot Rite, that even cubs are taught in few days after First Change? Why 2nd dot one is now?<br /> <br /> Also, I have multi-Tribe PCs pack - one (Alpha) Blood Talon, one Bone Shadow and two Hunters in Darkness. In game they are fighting with Bale Hounds pack. / For rare those that do not know them from 1ed - Bale Hounds are Uratha that works for Maeljins, Lords of Wounds, nasty types - their bosses are mentioned in sidebar on page 76 of 2ed corebook <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /> / So this is the Sacred Hunt question - <b>If PCs are going to face werewolves with help of Wounds spirits, can both Blood Talon and Bone Shadow make <i>Siskur-Dah</i> and they effect will work for other Prey? Can characters make those Rites in the one ceremony, to save time? What can Hunters in Darkness players do, if their Tribe do not follow particular Prey that will be Hunt?</b><br /> <br /> And another question - <b>How long Sacred Hunt works?</b> It do not have Duration aspect mentioned in write-up. <b>Can there be multiple <i>Siskur-Dah</i> Conditions on the same Uratha character, each for other Prey?</b>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:47:01-07:00","id":433157,"title":"","content":"1) Legitimately good question.<br /> <br /> 2) The Talons declare the Hunt on the Hounds, the Shadows declare a hunt on the Wound Spirits. Easy peasy.<br /> <br /> 3) The Hunt lasts until you or the prey is dead.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 03-08-2015, 06:41 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:56:26-07:00","id":433179,"title":"","content":"1) All werewolves start with two dots of rites. Sacred Hunt can be bought at the start with that","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T14:57:06-07:00","id":433182,"title":"","content":"Am bit tired at the moment, so don't have the energy for a full explanation of Siskur-Dah right now, but suffice to say that it's a rite because it's a <i>sacred hunt</i>. You are literally drawing on the laws of the Shadow that are an echo of the God of the Hunt's old place in the <i>Hisil</i>. This is a ritual behaviour, channeling through what you are but drawing on the wider Shadow for its power; you need to know the 'key' to unlock that ancient echo. To make it an innate ability and not a rite would, to my mind, cheapen the ritual and shamanic elements of werewolf existence. It's <i>powerful;</i> it's <i>meaningful</i>; it's not a cheap trick or piece of petty magic. It plugs right into what the werewolf is, yes, but it is also <i>external</i> to the werewolf at the same time. You are drawing on <i>laws of the hunt</i>. A hunt isn't sacred just because you say it is, you have to undertake the right actions to render it sacred.<br /> <br /> I'm honestly not sure how to parse your second set of queries - can you maybe rephrase them to be clearer? I think you're asking if a werewolf can have two <i>Siskur-Dah</i> Conditions at the same time, but then you seem to ask the same question again in the third set of queries?<br /> <br /> As to how long the Sacred Hunt lasts, the Resolution part of the Siskur-Dah Condition has all the info you need to know on that front.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T16:35:14-07:00","id":433266,"title":"","content":"I'm running a 2.0 game right now. I don't know if it is right, but this works like a charm:<br /> <br /> 1) The primary actor starts the Sacred Hunt ritual.<br /> 2) Any participant who also knows Sacred Hunt may add their tribal bonus.<br /> <br /> So if a Blood Talon and a Storm Lord both know Sacred Hunt, and both participate in the ritual, then the pack can see werewolf renown AND notice possessed, urged or claimed while they have the Siskur-Dah condition. Easy peasy.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":2273,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","user":"Incendax","date":". 03-08-2015, 07:49 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T16:51:08-07:00","id":433278,"title":"","content":"It might be a case of mechanics interfering in narrative to say otherwise ( and I am all for pushing story/feel/experience forward in that case ) but one of my favorite parts of siskur-dah is how personal it is. Going with that, I would say unless the other pack member in the above example is making rolls, they have no influence. I don't think I would care if it was 5 and 5 or ten each, but both need their skin in the game.<br /> <br /> I wrote up a character whom I would love to perform siskur-dah with a brawl+composure roll. Meditatively, stoically obliterating an effigy of their prey into dust, working up the pack as they feed off his silent fury, climaxing in an inspiring, victorious howl of glorious victory? That is some PERSONAL stuff going on there though..! Just because someone else is sharing the campfire you do that around, doesn't mean they are altering the experience, right? There is a certain amount of spotlight hogging needed to add your personal flavor to a rite, I would think.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":3070,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","user":"Barbrarilen","date":".  autocorrect....! 03-08-2015, 07:51 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3070-barbrarilen","name":"Barbrarilen","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3070_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"268"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T17:36:54-07:00","id":433333,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Incendax</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=433266#post433266\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'm running a 2.0 game right now. I don't know if it is right, but this works like a charm:<br /> <br /> 1) The primary actor starts the Sacred Hunt ritual.<br /> 2) Any participant who also knows Sacred Hunt may add their tribal bonus.<br /> <br /> So if a Blood Talon and a Storm Lord both know Sacred Hunt, and both participate in the ritual, then the pack can see werewolf renown AND notice possessed, urged or claimed while they have the Siskur-Dah condition. Easy peasy.</div> </div> </div> </div>AFAIK, that's an incorrect use. Though if it works for your game, more power to you.<br /> <br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T17:38:38-07:00","id":433334,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Barbrarilen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=433278#post433278\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It might be a case of mechanics interfering in narrative to say otherwise ( and I am all for pushing story/feel/experience forward in that case ) but one of my favorite parts of siskur-dah is how personal it is. Going with that, I would say unless the other pack member in the above example is making rolls, they have no influence. I don't think I would care if it was 5 and 5 or ten each, but both need their skin in the game.<br /> <br /> I wrote up a character whom I would love to perform siskur-dah with a brawl+composure roll. Meditatively, stoically obliterating an effigy of their prey into dust, working up the pack as they feed off his silent fury, climaxing in an inspiring, victorious howl of glorious victory? That is some PERSONAL stuff going on there though..! Just because someone else is sharing the campfire you do that around, doesn't mean they are altering the experience, right? There is a certain amount of spotlight hogging needed to add your personal flavor to a rite, I would think.</div> </div> </div> </div><i>Desert Dreaming Hunt</i> in the Idigam Anthology has two examples of very personalised Rites - including the <i>Siskur-Dah</i>.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T20:01:03-07:00","id":433495,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=433182#post433182\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Am bit tired at the moment, so don't have the energy for a full explanation of Siskur-Dah right now, but suffice to say that it's a rite because it's a <i>sacred hunt</i>. You are literally drawing on the laws of the Shadow that are an echo of the God of the Hunt's old place in the <i>Hisil</i>. This is a ritual behaviour, channeling through what you are but drawing on the wider Shadow for its power; you need to know the 'key' to unlock that ancient echo. To make it an innate ability and not a rite would, to my mind, cheapen the ritual and shamanic elements of werewolf existence. It's <i>powerful;</i> it's <i>meaningful</i>; it's not a cheap trick or piece of petty magic. It plugs right into what the werewolf is, yes, but it is also <i>external</i> to the werewolf at the same time. You are drawing on <i>laws of the hunt</i>. A hunt isn't sacred just because you say it is, you have to undertake the right actions to render it sacred.<br /> <br /> I'm honestly not sure how to parse your second set of queries - can you maybe rephrase them to be clearer? I think you're asking if a werewolf can have two <i>Siskur-Dah</i> Conditions at the same time, but then you seem to ask the same question again in the third set of queries?<br /> <br /> As to how long the Sacred Hunt lasts, the Resolution part of the Siskur-Dah Condition has all the info you need to know on that front.</div> </div> </div> </div>If they ever do a book similar to Lore of the Forsaken or Blood of the Wolf I would love to see you go in depth about the mystical and pshycological aspects of the rite Acrozatarim...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4055-felipe","name":"Felipe","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar4055_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"538"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T20:16:51-07:00","id":433507,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bunyip</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=433333#post433333\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">AAFAIK, that's an incorrect use. Though if it works for your game, more power to you.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes. Seems much simpler, easier to manager, more inclusive of other pack members who may want to contribute in any give hunt but cannot because their particular prey does not show up as often in a story, and fewer hard feelings &quot;Sorry Bob, we're don't need your sacred hunt again. Jane's is much more useful.&quot;<br /> <br /> It's still a brand new game / brand new house rule. So we'll see how it pans out over time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2273-incendax","name":"Incendax","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Feb 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"283"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-08T20:22:38-07:00","id":433538,"title":"","content":"Anyone can contribute in a sacred hunt. The sacred prey of a tribe is just something they focus on, it is not a limiter in any other way. A doctor has gone to medical school, but they can still try and fix a car or draw a cartoon, design a website. If something is disrupting their territory or worthy of a hunt, they'll hunt it even if it isn't any tribes sacred prey.<br /> <br /> This seems an odd sticking point for some readers.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 03-08-2015, 11:26 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":6}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T13:04:13-07:00","id":434436,"title":"","content":"Maybe because it isn't really explained very well.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\"><span style=\"font-family:Times New Roman\">The problem with defending the purity of the English language is that English is about as pure as a cribhouse whore. We don't just borrow words; on occasion, English has pursued other languages down alleyways to beat them unconscious and rifle their pockets for new vocabulary. - James. D. Nicoll</span></span></i>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/540-tymeaus-jalynsfein","name":"Tymeaus Jalynsfein","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"869"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T13:24:39-07:00","id":434464,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Tymeaus Jalynsfein</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=434436#post434436\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Maybe because it isn't really explained very well.</div> </div> </div> </div>People not understanding the difference between &quot;worthiest prey&quot; and &quot;only prey&quot; is pretty much entirely on their own heads.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":10}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-03-09T13:52:30-07:00","id":434486,"title":"","content":"The way I read it all, anyone could take the Siskur-Dah rite at character creation, but nobody in particular has to. What the rite does is start the hunt. What all of the werewolves need to do is go on such a hunt. One packmate can start it, everyone can go along. Everyone gets the condition, everyone fulfills there basic wolfy need.<br /> While anyone who knows the rite can call it on just about anything (be it a spirit to feed on for essence, a zoning proposal that needs to not pass legislation, or the Fire-Touched that killed your character's mom), the Tribal affiliation of the person leading the rite colors it to add strength against that Tribe's preferred prey. After all, it's what they've hunted more than anything else since time immemorial, so their hunts focus on that.<br /> <br /> Now, for the Bale hound hunt, it might be good to have someone from all three tribes know the rite and maybe find a way to have all three do the rituals in tandem. The Blood Talon can scout out the opponent wolves, the Bone Shadow can take on the supporting spirits, and the Hunter in Darkness can see and understand the wounds themselves more clearly. If only one of those things is called for, have everyone join in to help for whichever rite would help. If you need to do it all at once, your fourth man can assist with any of those three things you want, even though he's a Hunter in Darkness.<br /> <br /> As a pack, decide what you want to or expect to be hunting. Make sure the Tribes who hunt that are represented and know this rite. If you don't want to hunt other werewolves, or you just don't care about being sure of their Renown, then don't worry about having a Blood-Talon that knows it.<br /> Or, if you like dramatic tension, figure out what you'll be hunting and intentionally don't have the right Tribe with that rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","user":"TerraBen","date":". 03-09-2015, 04:55 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T23:26:11-07:00","id":472272,"title":"","content":"Other question that spring from mine Sweden game - <b>Can Siskur-Dah be called on group of beings?</b> Like can mine Bale Hounds pack declare whole Forsaken pack of PCs?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-07T23:59:28-07:00","id":472322,"title":"","content":"&quot;Let all thousand eyes watching be a witness to this vow: Either the Forest Nightmare pack dies, or we do&quot;.<br /> <br /> Or in other words, so long as it's specific sure, go for it.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":3}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T01:09:00-07:00","id":472354,"title":"","content":"You can literally call <i>Siskur-Dah</i> on anything you want. A person, a group of people, an object, an intangible concept, or anything else you can think of.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T04:33:47-07:00","id":472494,"title":"","content":"I've been trying to wrap my head around the continuity of a Siskur-Dah and what happens when you break it. The answers I've found so far are &quot;any significant action away from the siskur-dah revokes it.&quot; And &quot;there are no 'in game' penalties for breaking it'. Finally, it seems like the conclusion is pretty much when the pack says its done and can be a symbolic hunt as much as a real hunt. <br /> <br /> To me it feels stylized, but not very specific - so there's not a lot in consequences/rewards and not a lot of clear definition. I suppose one could say &quot;the hunt is its own reward!&quot; Which hey, that's fine since this is all about fun RP. Maybe I need to tap into my ten year old self and ask about 'cops &amp; robbas&quot;. <br /> <br /> Anyone else have any insight or opinions on this? <br /> <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T04:41:00-07:00","id":472498,"title":"","content":"I figured one major bonus for Siskur-dah was the amount of beats a group could be swimming in.<br /> <br /> Considering the amount of 8-agains, +Renown bonuses, and exceptional successes on three successes instead of five rules around. And that the Siskur-dah has you gaining a beat everytime you get an exceptional success.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/717-monghani","name":"Monghani","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar717_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"358"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T06:15:16-07:00","id":472619,"title":"","content":"What Monghani said. Also, remember that all level 3 Moon Gifts work only during Siskur-Dah, so that's another bonus and encouragement to continue the hunt until its bloody end.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/216-zooroos","name":"Zooroos","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar216_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"250"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T06:39:18-07:00","id":472635,"title":"","content":"I suppose if we ever get expansion on tribes it would be interesting to see more possible rewards from the Siskur-Dah, for taking down your sacred prey. Like maybe you could pull something from the shartha. Or perhaps you could throw a human's sacred prey into a sort of permanent Skin Thief alternative.<br /> <br /> I can understand why they didn't seem to really make specifically failing the hunt a point of failure, I think. Not everyone is going to use the hunt to kill a target, so it seems like you could just target, 'The one who kidnapped our packmate,' then upon finding out it was Dire Wolf decide that maybe you took the hunt far enough. But it would be interesting to see some ramifications for a pack that has failed many hunts. Though perhaps that's what the Predator Kings are for.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T08:26:19-07:00","id":472794,"title":"","content":"Next question that mine players will surely ask - <b>Can character have multiple Siskur-Dah Conditions on them?</b> Like Siskur-Dah (Blood Talons), Siskur-Dah(Bone Shadows) and Siskur-Dah (Hunters in Darkness) on the same character. <b>Or can there be one Siskur-Dah ritual, but many Ritemasters, each from different Tribe?</b> <b>Or does character can have only one Siskur-Dah and gains the benefits of his own Tribe, \u200bindependently of the Tribe of Ritemaster?</b><br /> <br /> Also - is Sacred Hunt on the concepts ( like certain law to pass ) is official ruling. Even if not, the Tribe bonuses would be added on to this Siskur-Dah?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T08:35:29-07:00","id":472824,"title":"","content":"The Siskur-Dah explicitly bestows the benefit of the Tribe of the ritemaster, not the Tribe of the werewolf subjected to it or the Tribe of any of the ritemaster's assistants in the ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T08:38:43-07:00","id":472846,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472794#post472794\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Next question that mine players will surely ask - <b>Can character have multiple Siskur-Dah Conditions on them?</b> Like Siskur-Dah (Blood Talons), Siskur-Dah(Bone Shadows) and Siskur-Dah (Hunters in Darkness) on the same character. <b>Or can there be one Siskur-Dah ritual, but many Ritemasters, each from different Tribe?</b> <b>Or does character can have only one Siskur-Dah and gains the benefits of his own Tribe, \u200bindependently of the Tribe of Ritemaster?</b><br /> <br /> Also - is Sacred Hunt on the concepts ( like certain law to pass ) is official ruling. Even if not, the Tribe bonuses would be added on to this Siskur-Dah?</div> </div> </div> </div>I wouldn't let players have multiple hunts active at the same time so no they could not have multiple Siskur-Dah Conditions at once. Characters gain the benefits of the rite master's tribe (p310).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":785,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","user":"Full Time GM","date":". 04-08-2015, 11:43 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:18:27-07:00","id":472899,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472824#post472824\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Siskur-Dah explicitly bestows the benefit of the Tribe of the ritemaster, not the Tribe of the werewolf subjected to it or the Tribe of any of the ritemaster's assistants in the ritual.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's a bummer, because it makes Blood Talons only suitable in the chronicle based on Bale Hounds, like mine game - and any other game based mostly on one antagonists group, is it Claimed, Hosts or even humans. You must have varied antagonists to not make characters down as each and single Siskur-Dah is about &quot;Joe favorite Prey&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> I hoped at least that various Tribes members could get various benefits - like Ritemaster activate the Siskur-Dah on his Prey, but still Blood Talon get the sight of Renown, Hunters in Darkness see the Gauntlet state, etc.<br /> <br /> I probably foreseen the house rule is coming...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:22:33-07:00","id":472908,"title":"","content":"If, as per your initial example, you need multiple benefits for the same hunt, decide beforehand which of your pack members are going to take care of which threats. Then have people from each tribe perform the Rite affecting the different teams.<br /> Note that the Storm Lord, Hunter in Darkness, and Blood Talon benefits are laregely for information gathering. If you have good communication within your pack, one person with any of those will do. The Bone Shadow benefit should be bestowed on anyone that needs to hit a spirit. The Iron Masters one should go on anyone who expects to shift in front of humans during the hunt.<br /> This brings up an interesting point: if two people with the Iron Masters benefit go Urshul in front of someone but pick different Lunacy conditions, is it a normal Clash of Will situation or is there some other way to determine what would happen?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:24:54-07:00","id":472911,"title":"","content":"Or Pure, or Ghost Wolves, or Forsaken who've broken the Oath of the Moon. Plus a Blood Talon can call a Siskur-Dah on anything, just like everyone else. They just won't be able to see Renown brands on everything.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:33:29-07:00","id":472915,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472899#post472899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's a bummer, because it makes Blood Talons only suitable in the chronicle based on Bale Hounds, like mine game - and any other game based mostly on one antagonists group, is it Claimed, Hosts or even humans. You must have varied antagonists to not make characters down as each and single Siskur-Dah is about &quot;Joe favorite Prey&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>What? Why? The Blood Talon Siskur-Dah benefit is useful when hunting any werewolves. Bale hounds, pure, ghost wolves, other Uratha that pissed you off... Arguably <i>Su'ur</i>... And even when you're hunting something else, there are other benefits to being a Blood Talon, like easier access to their Tribal Gifts. Varied antagonists is supposed to be the default. If you want to tell a story that only features one group of antagonist, or that features one group far more prominently than others, discuss that with your players in session 0 so they can plan accordingly.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472899#post472899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I hoped at least that various Tribes members could get various benefits - like Ritemaster activate the Siskur-Dah on his Prey, but still Blood Talon get the sight of Renown, Hunters in Darkness see the Gauntlet state, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Why would you even need those benefits if you weren't hunting that tribe's prey? Seeing your prey's Renown is useless if your prey isn't a werewolf and therefore doesn't have renown. Seeing the gauntlet strength is only useful if you expect the gauntlet strength to actually change. Damaging spirits in twilight form is only useful against spirits and nothing else. Seeing what lunacy conditions are affecting your prey does nothing unless your prey is actually susceptible to lunacy. Being able to see the spirit Urging or Claiming your prey doesn't do anything if your prey isn't Urged or Claimed.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472899#post472899\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I probably foreseen the house rule is coming...</div> </div> </div> </div>What ever floats your boat, but I don't see this house rule as actually doing anything.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":269,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","user":"Charlaquin","date":". 04-08-2015, 12:40 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:41:40-07:00","id":472925,"title":"","content":"If you've only got one antagonist, or if there are other antogonists around but your pack is only planning to fight one thing, then you're kindof in a great situation. Just have someone of the appropriate Tribe learn the Siskur-Dah Rite, then have everyone else learn different Rites. The Rite for defining your pack's territory is a 2-dot Rite that your pack won't know if everyone takes Siskur-Dah with their 2 points at creation. There are a lot of other really handy one and two dot Rites out there that open wide up if you don't need the various Tribe bonuses on your hunt. If your hunts won't cross paths with the Claimed, any Storm Lords in your pack have no compulsion to perform (and thus even know) the Siskur-Dah Rite.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T09:49:42-07:00","id":472939,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472908#post472908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If, as per your initial example, you need multiple benefits for the same hunt, decide beforehand which of your pack members are going to take care of which threats. Then have people from each tribe perform the Rite affecting the different teams.</div> </div> </div> </div>No, I would rather want different benefits from the same Sacred Hunt. Mine PCs pack is lead by Blood Talon, have also Bone Shadow and Hunters in Darkness. <i><b>Whole chronicle</b></i> is based on idea they fight the Bale Hounds pack. If PCs need to take one of Hounds, Blood Talon would be Ritemaster. The next one of Hounds - Blood Talon would be Ritemaster. And a like, and like this. Every time, only one player lead the hunt. And characters get only benefits of Blood Talons, not their Tribes.<br /> <br /> Sure I can throw an episode of spirit hunt or Hosts threat - but the<b><i> idea of chronicle</i></b> is Bale Hounds pack and it's threat. Other PCs will shine as Ritemasters once, maybe twice in the game - and all the rest of time the Blood Talon will get the lead and &quot;cool powers&quot;.<br /> <br /> Problem is that I could see Hunters in Darkness Siskur-Dah benefit as interesting and valuable, but PCs would not get this, as they all hunt enemy werewolves.<br /> <br /> I have now idea of house rule: <b>Character under Siskur-Dah get's his Tribe benefit <i>and</i> Ritemasters.</b> So Hunters in Darkness on Hunt are always attuned to Gaunlet, Bone Shadows can hit ephemera, etc. And in mine example, all of them would see the Renown Brands of the prey.<br /> <br /> Because alternative is that only the Blood Talons benefit is almost all the time active, or each Tribe in the pack is making their own Siskur-Dah each time, so we have three Sacred Hunts at the same time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472908#post472908\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Note that the Storm Lord, Hunter in Darkness, and Blood Talon benefits are laregely for information gathering. If you have good communication within your pack, one person with any of those will do. The Bone Shadow benefit should be bestowed on anyone that needs to hit a spirit. The Iron Masters one should go on anyone who expects to shift in front of humans during the hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>We then still have &quot;one actor show&quot; as &quot;correct&quot; Tribe member will say all the time &quot;oh, he has Glory on 4 and Purity on 3. And she has Wisdom on 2.&quot; - and he talks like this all the time.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472911#post472911\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Or Pure, or Ghost Wolves, or Forsaken who've broken the Oath of the Moon. Plus a Blood Talon can call a Siskur-Dah on anything, just like everyone else. They just won't be able to see Renown brands on everything.</div> </div> </div> </div>This is also mine confusion - <b>Is Tribal benefit for Siskur-Dah working at any Sacred Hunt, or only those on Tribes Favorite Prey?</b> So in our example, if Blood Talon's Sacred Hunt giving sight of Renown even when we are not hunting other werewolves, but let's say a new law?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:01:27-07:00","id":472954,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472915#post472915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What? Why? The Blood Talon Siskur-Dah benefit is useful when hunting any werewolves. Bale hounds, pure, ghost wolves, other Uratha that pissed you off... Arguably <i>Su'ur</i>... And even when you're hunting something else, there are other benefits to being a Blood Talon, like easier access to their Tribal Gifts. Varied antagonists is supposed to be the default. If you want to tell a story that only features one group of antagonist, or that features one group far more prominently than others, discuss that with your players in session 0 so they can plan accordingly.</div> </div> </div> </div>Idea was that they would not plan they character, as they would not know the threat. It's like making ST to spill the beans of chronicle - &quot;Hey, huys, I have a plot and it will be mostly about Bale Hounds, so better take Blood Talons.&quot; - Where is suspens in that? It's also making player to make desicion based on the future plot threat, not his own idea of character - &quot;I would want to play urban explorer Hunter in Darkness. - No, Steve, we are making Bale Hounds chronicle, you must choose Blood Talon, or you would not make many Rites in the game.&quot; It's a bit like &quot;possible plot blackmail&quot;. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/confused.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Confused\" smilieid=\"10\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472915#post472915\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Why would you even need those benefits if you weren't hunting that tribe's prey? Seeing your prey's Renown is useless if your prey isn't a werewolf and therefore doesn't have renown. Seeing the gauntlet strength is only useful if you expect the gauntlet strength to actually change. Damaging spirits in twilight form is only useful against spirits and nothing else. Seeing what lunacy conditions are affecting your prey does nothing unless your prey is actually susceptible to lunacy. Being able to see the spirit Urging or Claiming your prey doesn't do anything if your prey isn't Urged or Claimed.</div> </div> </div> </div>Even if you hunt the Hosts or spirits, you can come across other werewolves, and then Renown could be useful. Seeing Gauntlet strength in area that should normally have other - like dense Gauntlet in wilderness - give you info that there are other process behind the curtain, not only generated by Hosts - like Uratha could making Shadow Engineering. And Bone Shadows benefit grants you attacks based on <b>any</b> ephemera being, not only spirits. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> Those benefits are very usefull even when you are not hunting the Tribes prey.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:02:38-07:00","id":472970,"title":"","content":"Starting from the bottom, yes. If your pack is on the proverbial zoning-law hunt and the Rite was led by your Blood Talon, you'd see quite clearly that the lawyer pulling the strings is a werewolf in Hishu form with 5 dots of Cunning and 2 dots of Wisdom. At least that's how I'd take it.<br /> <br /> As to most of the rest of your questions, why do the other players need to run the Siskur-Dah Rite? If your Blood-Talon did the Rite, then everyone would see for themselves what Renown their prey are sporting and your Blood-Talon wouldn't need to be all chatty about it. You as the GM could announce it to the table.<br /> Leading the Siskur-Dah Rite doesn't necessarily mean that you are the leader of the hunt itself, or that the whole thing is your show. If your Blood-Talon is particularly good at using Gauru form, then he should probably be the one to do the killing most of the time, but there's more to the fight than just the kill. There's a lot of teamwork that goes into it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:11:09-07:00","id":472997,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472939#post472939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">No, I would rather want different benefits from the same Sacred Hunt. Mine PCs pack is lead by Blood Talon, have also Bone Shadow and Hunters in Darkness. <i><b>Whole chronicle</b></i> is based on idea they fight the Bale Hounds pack. If PCs need to take one of Hounds, Blood Talon would be Ritemaster. The next one of Hounds - Blood Talon would be Ritemaster. And a like, and like this. Every time, only one player lead the hunt. And characters get only benefits of Blood Talons, not their Tribes.</div> </div> </div> </div>If all you're hunting is Bale Hounds, those other benefits would be useless anyway.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472939#post472939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure I can throw an episode of spirit hunt or Hosts threat - but the<b><i> idea of chronicle</i></b> is Bale Hounds pack and it's threat. Other PCs will shine as Ritemasters once, maybe twice in the game - and all the rest of time the Blood Talon will get the lead and &amp;quot;cool powers&amp;quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>Then they're free to spend those dots on other rites and shine in other areas. The hunter in darkness can be the one responsible for being the ritemaster on the Hunting Ground rite, maintaining the pack's territory. The Bone Shadow can be the go-to ritemaster for Wellspring, strengthening the pack's Loci. The Iron Master can be in charge of performing Moon's Mad Love so the human pack members aren't constantly vulnerable to lunacy. The Storm Lord can take Totemic Empowerment to beef himself up and Harness the Cycle for an extra source of essence. Besides, since everyone gets the same benefits from Siskur-Dah, who really cares who the ritemaster is?<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472939#post472939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Problem is that I could see Hunters in Darkness Siskur-Dah benefit as interesting and valuable, but PCs would not get this, as they all hunt enemy werewolves.</div> </div> </div> </div>But what use would it even be if all you're hunting is werewolves? Werewolves don't change the gauntlet strength, so if you find out what it is once, you pretty much always know what it is, as long as no <i>Sartha</i> show up.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472939#post472939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I have now idea of house rule: <b>Character under Siskur-Dah get's his Tribe benefit <i>and</i> Ritemasters.</b> So Hunters in Darkness on Hunt are always attuned to Gaunlet, Bone Shadows can hit ephemera, etc. And in mine example, all of them would see the Renown Brands of the prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>I still don't see how that would make any functional difference. If you aren't hunting <i>Sartha</i> you don't need to see the gauntlet strength. If you aren't hunting spirits, you don't need to be able to hit spirits. The various <i>Siskur-Dah</i> benefits don't really do anything to help you against a different kind of prey.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472939#post472939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Because alternative is that only the Blood Talons benefit is almost all the time active, or each Tribe in the pack is making their own Siskur-Dah each time, so we have three Sacred Hunts at the same time. <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/frown.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Frown\" smilieid=\"11\" class=\"inlineimg\" /></div> </div> </div> </div>If all you're hunting is Bale Hounds, having the blood talon benefit all the time is exactly what you'd want.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472939#post472939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">We then still have &amp;quot;one actor show&amp;quot; as &amp;quot;correct&amp;quot; Tribe member will say all the time &amp;quot;oh, he has Glory on 4 and Purity on 3. And she has Wisdom on 2.&amp;quot; - and he talks like this all the time.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't see the problem here. That's not scene stealing, it's just effective teamwork.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472939#post472939\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">This is also mine confusion - <b>Is Tribal benefit for Siskur-Dah working at any Sacred Hunt, or only those on Tribes Favorite Prey?</b> So in our example, if Blood Talon's Sacred Hunt giving sight of Renown even when we are not hunting other werewolves, but let's say a new law?</div> </div> </div> </div>The benefit that applies is based on who performed the rite, nor what the prey is. Though, like I've been saying, they're so specialized, they aren't of much use against any other kind of prey.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:33:32-07:00","id":473018,"title":"","content":"Oh no, Ham's throwing things wildly out of proportion again.<br /> <br /> In other news, Seattle really loves coffee.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":5}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:39:50-07:00","id":473022,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=473018#post473018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh no, Ham's throwing things wildly out of proportion again.<br /> <br /> In other news, Seattle really loves coffee.</div> </div> </div> </div>Thank you for that moment of perspective.<br /> <br /> I think a lot of this arguement does come down to the question: &quot;Why does it seem like such a big deal to be the Rite master?&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:40:49-07:00","id":473025,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=473018#post473018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Oh no, Ham's throwing things wildly out of proportion again.<br /> <br /> In other news, Seattle really loves coffee.</div> </div> </div> </div><span style=\"color:red\">That was uncalled for.</span>","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:55:23-07:00","id":473051,"title":"","content":"I'd like to point out that nothing requires the rite master to &quot;lead&quot; the hunt. That character just does the blessing of the rite, they don't have to be the person at the front of the pack the whole time.<br /> <br /> When I had my players make their characters I told them it would be a good idea for them to check who was playing what tribe and for at least one member of each tribe to have the Sacred Hunt rite so that they'd be able to invoke whichever one they might need at the given time. That worked perfectly well.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T10:58:30-07:00","id":473054,"title":"","content":"Yeah, you're right. Sorry Ham, that was uncalled for. I'm grouchy when I wake up.<br /> <br /> But in seriousness now, putting aside some design choices I question that I'll get back to later, the Talon might lead against the main antagonists, but that doesn't make him the ritemaster/leader, that makes him the high useful specialist. In all reality, everyone else is going to be good at rites pertinent to what they're doing in the pack, and it's not like you need the other rite effects against the Hounds.<br /> <br /> But more on point, you say you're hunting Bale Hounds like they exist in a vacuum. They don't. For starters, the Hounds work with using and subverting spirits-they pollute the environment with the Infernal/Negative Essence, they craft the local choirs to their liking, they cow them into spying on the Forsaken and other targets. Same thing with humans, they get them to generate essence and otherwise provide resources and information-the Hounds control them like the spirits in order to control the land. And the intersection between them is bound to happen, to generate shit and and overload the Forsaken and other parties and throw them off the scent, so the Claimed are going to be a big part of their plans. THe only ones who they can't use directly are the Shartha, and they can still take advantage of any local Shartha doing their schtick.<br /> <br /> So my big question is &quot;Why would your pack only learn the Talon's Siskur-Dah when they have an entire network and structure that stands in the way of them?&quot;.<br /> <br /> Let the Bone Shadows take the Hounds Totem and spirit allies, let the Hunters track down the lose ends, give them allies who can lead against the humans and the Claimed while still relying on them to take charge over the operation. Never a problem, always a solution, You have plenty of tools to make this work without having to turn the Siskur-Dah into an overpowered rite by having <i>everything </i>go off.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T11:08:52-07:00","id":473067,"title":"","content":"If they're not too off-topic, I would be interested in hearing your questions about the design choices, Arcane. When you have time to properly articulate them, of course.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T11:23:09-07:00","id":473087,"title":"","content":"I brought them up after that paragraph-I wanted to reiterate what you said before asking about the design of the campaign.<br /> <br /> Particularly given the extension of packs and the tools given to make them bigger movers, Werewolf is now, more than ever, a game of controlling the terrain. You have a pack that can includes spirits, humans, stranger things still, and even beyond that you can manipulate all aspects of the modern/spiritual ecosystem to create your vision of a harmonized territory.<br /> <br /> The Forsaken don't just hunt humans, they use them! They get them to picket and riot and fund and steal and listen and watch.<br /> The Forsaken don't just hunt spirits, they use them! They get them to cultivate and misdirect and bargain and haunt and listen and watch.<br /> The Forsaken don't just hunt shartha, they use them! They shove them around and herd them to strengthen the gauntlet where they wants and weaken it where they wants, shapign the environment, before they try to kill them.<br /> <br /> The Claimed and the Uratha are the ones least likely to be used, but 2nd Edition doesn't just ramp up the fact that werewolves hunt these things, it ramps up that they manipulate them to better grasp their territory. (In regards to the claimed, consider that the Forsaken skirt this by having rituals that make temporary Claimed, as an example)<br /> <br /> And that's <i>just</i> the good guys! The Bale Hounds, in fact, have to go and create networks and structures and manipulate their territory like this even more so than the Forsaken because of the particulars they depend on. When you say &quot;This game is built around hunting a Bale Hound pack&quot;, you have to acknowledge all the things that pack is doing in order to make things work, which includes a lot of things that <i>aren't</i> Bale Hounds.<br /> <br /> Forsaken 2nd Edition really hammers in an awareness of ecosystem and food web, that things have their place in relation to each other.<br /> <br /> And quite frankly, I also have to ask why there's a blatant Bale Hound pack, considering they play the sneaky sneak slip into other packs, subvert their lives and corrupt animals into falling, but that's not the factor I've honed in on.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":7}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T14:53:15-07:00","id":473382,"title":"","content":"So what would you folks say would happen if you reneged on your Siskur-Dah? Whether through cowardice or pragmatism, this hunt is a bad idea and the pack decides to abandon it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T14:58:32-07:00","id":473390,"title":"","content":"It ends. That's listed as one of the ways to end the condition. I think it still counts. Nobody's expecting a 100% success rate.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T15:10:40-07:00","id":473405,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=473382#post473382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what would you folks say would happen if you reneged on your Siskur-Dah? Whether through cowardice or pragmatism, this hunt is a bad idea and the pack decides to abandon it.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think anything happens for ending the sacred hunt <i>per se, </i>beyond the <i>Siskur-Dah</i> Condition resolving, obviously. But depending on the specifics of the situation that lead to the hunt being called off, it might be a sign of weakness, which is bad news for any <i>Imnir</i> in the pack. A particularly strict <i>Suthar Anzuth</i> might see it as a form of surrender. A <i>Meninna </i>that ends a hunt on her territory prematurely could be seen as a violation of <i>mus-rah</i>. If it was a spirit you were hunting, not completing the hunt could mean the pack's <i>Hifathra Hissu</i> may not be able to pay it in kind. And a <i>Farsil Luhal's</i> prey could bring dishonor or harm to her territory if allowed to escape. Depending on the pack Totem's Ban, it may not appreicate letting the prey go. There is a lot of potential for indirect consequences without there being a specific penalty for failure tied to the Rite or the Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T16:22:43-07:00","id":473493,"title":"","content":"Nofather and I discussed Siskur-Dah quite a bit today. To be fair, he doesn't agree with all my opinions, but he was great for bouncing ideas off of. <br /> <br /> Here's what I came up with: <br /> <br /> Siskur-Dah should be started with an intention of how the hunt will be ended. Whether this is &quot;find&quot; the prey, &quot;kill&quot; the prey, &quot;kiss&quot; the prey. Whatever it is. But when you initiate the rite, you declare or make known your intentions. Then, this is the intention you must fulfill to complete the hunt . <br /> <br /> So if you start off going to kill your prey, but wimp out at the end cause it winds up being Rambo - then you can't declare &quot;Well, we found him anyway&quot; and call off the hunt and consider it 'successful'.<br /> <br /> The second part is what consequences are suffered when you abandon the hunt (which is really the only way to 'fail' a hunt, is to give up). <br /> <br /> We considered a lot of options, but this is what I like: As a wolf, you hunt . Spirits know this. The wolf must hunt. SO! If you declare siskur-dah and fail to complete it, you'll start earning a bad rep among the spirits. Fail once and maybe it's not a big deal, but fail a lot and they may start considering you &quot;toothless&quot;. They may demand higher chiminage or just feel they can ignore you utterly. On the other hand, if you complete each hunt you start - that'll get you a rep too. No one will want to be on your bad side eh? <br /> <br /> So my next step for playing is to think about some more formalized rules to follow that concept. I've never been terribly interested in a 'homebrew', but I guess this would count.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T17:17:41-07:00","id":473527,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Elfive</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=473390#post473390\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It ends. That's listed as one of the ways to end the condition. I think it still counts. Nobody's expecting a 100% success rate.</div> </div> </div> </div>This isn't a rules dispute, we all know how it works.<br /> <br /> The Uratha are part spirit, and spirits do what spirits do. They come from the Predators Paradise. What happens to a spirit that doesn't want enough? It gets gobbled up by other spirits that do. But mechanically and fluff-wise, very little happens to werewolves when they give up the hunt, fail at the hunt, are fickle about the hunt, or just have eyes to big for their mouths. Rules as written, you even get a beat for resolving the Siskur-Dah condition by just breaking off the hunt, putting one failure of a pack at the same place as a pack that managed to bring down ISIS, for example.<br /> <br /> Mother's Love suggested the 'toothless' condition, and I do think the spirits having a lesser opinion of the pack should be a part of it, but I also would like more depth to the Effective Spirit Rank aspect of the game. I was thinking in the case of a failed hunt, where the prey not only manages to get away but trounces or humiliates the pack, the Demoralized condition may work.<br /> <br /> I'm just putting this out there to see if anyone has any ideas for something to do in-game in the case of a failed hunt. And proposing that if Werewolf gets further books, this is something that could be explored, since we do have writers and developers who peruse these boards.<br /> <br /> Though I will add that I do think a reward for a successful Siskur-Dah against a tribe's sacred prey could be an interesting idea. As is, you only get a real benefit if you tackle a spirit. I wouldn't want it to come off mercenary, but it could add an interesting facet to pack dynamics if the 'alpha' of the pack or whoever decides had to keep in mind the needs of other members, and other members had more reason to stand up and demand their sacred prey be hunted. Plus it might put more meaning behind the term 'sacred prey,' which a lot of people, not just here, seem to misunderstand.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T18:16:59-07:00","id":473573,"title":"","content":"Personally, I think the potential indirect consequences are plenty, no need for a Condition to codify it. To each their own, though.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T18:32:58-07:00","id":473586,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=473573#post473573\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Personally, I think the potential indirect consequences are plenty, no need for a Condition to codify it. To each their own, though.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> You don't think they should even spend a sentence more expanding on potential indirect consequences? Because currently the only one mentioned in the book seems to be the target lives and keeps doing what they're doing.<br /> <br /> You don't think there should be conditions, that's great, but what does potential indirect consequences consist of beyond the prey doing what they were doing? And does that mean there should be no consequences to failing a non-lethal hunt?<br /> <br /> Trying to get some dialogue here. Ideas.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-08-2015, 09:35 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T18:36:54-07:00","id":473587,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=473586#post473586\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You don't think they should even spend a sentence more expanding on potential indirect consequences? Because currently the only one seems to be the target lives and keeps doing what they're doing.</div> </div> </div> </div>To reiterate,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>me, a few posts ago</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\">...depending on the specifics of the situation that lead to the hunt being called off, it might be a sign of weakness, which is bad news for any <i>Imnir</i> in the pack. A particularly strict <i>Suthar Anzuth</i> might see it as a form of surrender. A <i>Meninna </i>that ends a hunt on her territory prematurely could be seen as a violation of <i>mus-rah</i>. If it was a spirit you were hunting, not completing the hunt could mean the pack's <i>Hifathra Hissu</i> may not be able to pay it in kind. And a <i>Farsil Luhal's</i> prey could bring dishonor or harm to her territory if allowed to escape. Depending on the pack Totem's Ban, it may not appreicate letting the prey go...</div> </div> </div> </div>just to name a few.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T18:41:33-07:00","id":473591,"title":"","content":"See, that's what I'm talking about.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T19:38:19-07:00","id":473675,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=473382#post473382\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">So what would you folks say would happen if you reneged on your Siskur-Dah? Whether through cowardice or pragmatism, this hunt is a bad idea and the pack decides to abandon it.</div> </div> </div> </div>Nobody is gonna talk about the Breaking Point towards Flesh that happens when you don't complete a hunt?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T19:51:25-07:00","id":473692,"title":"","content":"Charlaquin has some really good points. I'd like to take a moment to chime in about the wait of &quot;the target lives and keeps doing what they're doing.&quot;<br /> It's a sacred hunt. If you called it, there was a reason for it. Most of the time, it's because something needed to be stopped or otherwise go down. In the case discussed earlier of the semi-unknown prey that turned out to be Rambo, why were you hunting Rambo in the first place? Is it because he kidnapped a pack mate? Did he kill them? Is he going to do it again? If he lives and keeps doing what he's doing, more of your loved ones die. Or more of your territory gets destroyed. Or more of your allies turn against you.<br /> <br /> Now sometimes the stakes aren't that high. The wolf must hunt, this is establshed by theme and by Primal Urge mechanics. As such, sometimes you sacredly hunt &quot;that tasty deer spirit I saw last week that looked ripe with essence&quot;. To do the whole sacred thing right, you need to wait until you're ready to focus solely on that hunt (any major actions to anything else does end the Siskur-Dah Condition, after all...) and then focus on that. But what if something that seems more pressing comes up? You don't honestly care if that deer spirit gets away. You weren't really going to kill it, after all; spirits come back after a couple of days if you don't devour all their essence and corpus and you had no reason to do that. <br /> The main in-book consequence to this softball scenario is that it's a breaking point towards flesh. Right out of character creation those are dangerous things. Later on, maybe that would be helpful. By then, though, you might well have a much higher Primal Urge and maybe you really did need to finish that hunt or start feeling the essence-starvation.<br /> <br /> In short I see a handful of bad thing that could come of skipping out on a hunt. Piling on a couple conditions to make it really clear to the players probably wouldn't hurt, but I bet an ST could make them feel it without them if they wanted to. I like the conditions idea; I don't know that the game demands it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T20:25:46-07:00","id":473782,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Ephsy</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=473675#post473675\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nobody is gonna talk about the Breaking Point towards Flesh that happens when you don't complete a hunt?</div> </div> </div> </div>I think you're talking about 'Refusing to participate in Siskur-Dah' on the Harmony page?<br /> <br /> It's not really about not doing it. Not doing the hunt at all has mechanical disadvantages. You start losing essence each day. I'm more concerned with failing or dishonoring the hunt you've participated in.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T22:06:24-07:00","id":473870,"title":"","content":"THere's no failing or dishonoring a Siskur-Dah, it's duration is &quot;Until Success&quot;. If you declare Siskur-Dah, you either kill the fuck or die trying. If you fail, you keep trying until one of those two things happen.<br /> <br /> EDIT: Like, I think this is something I hope people understand: Declaring a Sacred Hunt is <i>serious business</i>. You don't just causally do it, you commit when something has to, in your eyes, <i>irrevocably die</i>. When <i>no other option</i> will do. They die, or you die-that's <i>literally</i> the scale of importance the declaration of a Sacred Hunt is.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":99,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","user":"ArcaneArts","date":". 04-09-2015, 01:13 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T22:12:42-07:00","id":473877,"title":"","content":"The Condition for it offers an out.<br /> <br /> 'Resolution: The prey is brought down (a kill is not necessary) or the pack breaks off the Siskur-Dah by taking any significant actions towards ends other than the hunt.'","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-08T22:22:18-07:00","id":473885,"title":"","content":"AH, no! My memory has betrayed me!<br /> <br /> This is what I get for getting wrapped up in Sothis Ascends.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T00:12:03-07:00","id":473948,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472997#post472997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Then they're free to spend those dots on other rites and shine in other areas. The hunter in darkness can be the one responsible for being the ritemaster on the Hunting Ground rite, maintaining the pack's territory. The Bone Shadow can be the go-to ritemaster for Wellspring, strengthening the pack's Loci. The Iron Master can be in charge of performing Moon's Mad Love so the human pack members aren't constantly vulnerable to lunacy. The Storm Lord can take Totemic Empowerment to beef himself up and Harness the Cycle for an extra source of essence. Besides, since everyone gets the same benefits from Siskur-Dah, who really cares who the ritemaster is?</div> </div> </div> </div>All the example above are really good and I get the meaning of this. Only one more question - by the same benefit you mean that Ritemasters Tribal benefit will be in place? The idea is that there should be some lighting of other Tribes benefits here.<br /> <br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472997#post472997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">But what use would it even be if all you're hunting is werewolves? Werewolves don't change the gauntlet strength, so if you find out what it is once, you pretty much always know what it is, as long as no <i>Sartha</i> show up.</div> </div> </div> </div>Huh, really? I got impression from 1ED &quot;Shadow engineering&quot; in corebook Appendix that packs are strengthening or lowering Gaunlet in various points of they territory. Like in mine example, Bale Hounds Ithaeur can lower Gaunlet in Wound he created to easier the Maeljinn's spirits passing and controlling of physical world and humans.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472997#post472997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I still don't see how that would make any functional difference. If you aren't hunting <i>Sartha</i> you don't need to see the gauntlet strength. If you aren't hunting spirits, you don't need to be able to hit spirits. The various <i>Siskur-Dah</i> benefits don't really do anything to help you against a different kind of prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>For first, see above. For second - even when you are hunting werewolves, there possibly can be spirits guardians or alliances. Not to mentioned most often Totem will help them. So I say the Bone Shadows benefit is rather useful, especially in animist setting of <b>Werewolf</b> game. Also, Bone Shadows benefit can let you hit ephemeral beings, not only spirits - useful, if there are some unplanned difficulties like angry ghost, or God Machine angels in the mix of the hunting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472997#post472997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">If all you're hunting is Bale Hounds, having the blood talon benefit all the time is exactly what you'd want.<br /> <br /> I don't see the problem here. That's not scene stealing, it's just effective teamwork.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but maybe not only. And having all the time active Blood Talons benefit post a larger spotlight on Blood Talons in mixed Tribe pack. There is difference when you make Siskur-Dah for each Tribe on each other session. And there is if Blood Talons benefit is making 80% of Sacred Hunts Rites. but then, other pack members can specialize in other Rites,<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=472997#post472997\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The benefit that applies is based on who performed the rite, nor what the prey is. Though, like I've been saying, they're so specialized, they aren't of much use against any other kind of prey.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not agreeing on this fully, but acknowledge the ruling.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T02:45:18-07:00","id":474017,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=473870#post473870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Like, I think this is something I hope people understand: Declaring a Sacred Hunt is <i>serious business</i>. You don't just causally do it, you commit when something has to, in your eyes, <i>irrevocably die</i>. When <i>no other option</i> will do. They die, or you die-that's <i>literally</i> the scale of importance the declaration of a Sacred Hunt is.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think it's this &quot;serious business&quot; thing I want emphasized in my games. I agree with everyone who feels it can be run with the current rules satisfactorily - the rules leave plenty of space for different interpretations and I'm curious as to how other ST's are treating siskur-dah.<br /> <br /> My thought is that siskur-dah is a social and spiritual construct as well as a base urge and it can cause you to lose or gain face depending on how well its performed. I think it has a flavor of Changeling's oaths with its formal rite to start, maybe that's why i feel a need for some immediate, even supernatural consequence when abandoning it. <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5220-mother-s-love","name":"Mother's Love","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar5220_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Mar 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"58"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T09:20:00-07:00","id":474392,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=473870#post473870\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">EDIT: Like, I think this is something I hope people understand: Declaring a Sacred Hunt is <i>serious business</i>. You don't just causally do it, you commit when something has to, in your eyes, <i>irrevocably die</i>. When <i>no other option</i> will do. They die, or you die-that's <i>literally</i> the scale of importance the declaration of a Sacred Hunt is.</div> </div> </div> </div>Well, not necessarily <i>die</i> \u2014 we had that whole point of confusion arise about that, remember \u2014 but &quot;properly&quot; speaking, you're definitely declaring the Hunt to make <i>some</i> sort of hopefully-lasting change with regards to your prey.<br /> <br /> I think the more broadly applicable aspect would be the fact that as a rite the Sacred Hunt is engaging supernatural law and effectively constitutes an oath to pursue your target unto its seizure, destruction, etc.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><span style=\"font-family:trebuchet ms\"><span style=\"color:#4B0082\"><b>Resident Lore-Hound</b></span><br /> Currently Consuming: <i>Demon: the Descent 1e</i></span>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/111-satchel","name":"Satchel","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar111_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9828"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T09:23:59-07:00","id":474393,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=473782#post473782\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> I think you're talking about 'Refusing to participate in Siskur-Dah' on the Harmony page?<br /> <br /> It's not really about not doing it. Not doing the hunt at all has mechanical disadvantages. You start losing essence each day. I'm more concerned with failing or dishonoring the hunt you've participated in.</div> </div> </div> </div>It was <i>supposed</i> to inflict a Breaking Point towards Flesh if you broke off a Sacred Hunt. However, I now can't find where that was written, so it may have been edited out of the final text.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T09:26:29-07:00","id":474397,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Satchel</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=474392#post474392\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Well, not necessarily <i>die</i> \u2014 we had that whole point of confusion arise about that, remember \u2014 but &quot;properly&quot; speaking, you're definitely declaring the Hunt to make <i>some</i> sort of hopefully-lasting change with regards to your prey.<br /> <br /> I think the more broadly applicable aspect would be the fact that as a rite the Sacred Hunt is engaging supernatural law and effectively constitutes an oath to pursue your target unto its seizure, destruction, etc.</div> </div> </div> </div>Again, my memory betrayed me.<br /> <br /> I need some more Sebayt before I next declare that the point of the Forsaken is to raise cute bunnies.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T09:32:48-07:00","id":474400,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>ArcaneArts</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=474397#post474397\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Again, my memory betrayed me.<br /> <br /> I need some more Sebayt before I next declare that the point of the Forsaken is to raise cute bunnies.</div> </div> </div> </div>Is....is that not the point?<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>&quot;<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/127887-doing-first-tongue-translations?p=484226#post484226\" target=\"_blank\">Nihhina kalekal-zidu kal masun, kal manudanadu. Nihhina kalekal-zidu nukal shaghu-desasudu \u2014 nihhina kalekal-zidu kal innu-desasudu udhkal samm</a>.&quot; Arthur Ashe<br /> She/her, contributing writer for <a href=\"https://www.drivethrurpg.com/product/363404/Scion-Pride-2021\" target=\"_blank\">Scion: Pride 2021</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1923-bigdamnhero","name":"BigDamnHero","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1923_4.jpg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1263"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T09:46:25-07:00","id":474413,"title":"","content":"It is not.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Kelly R.S. Steele, Freelance Writer(Feel free to call me Kelly, Arcane, or Arc)</b><br /> The world is not beautiful, therefore it is.-Keiichi Sigsawa, Kino's Journey<br /> Feminine pronouns, please.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/99-arcanearts","name":"ArcaneArts","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar99_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11384"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T09:57:04-07:00","id":474428,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=474393#post474393\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It was <i>supposed</i> to inflict a Breaking Point towards Flesh if you broke off a Sacred Hunt. However, I now can't find where that was written, so it may have been edited out of the final text.</div> </div> </div> </div>I did see this the other day when I was commenting on it. I don't recall where exactly I saw it, but it is still in there. Somewhere.<br /> <br /> The other thing I remember more clearly is that failing to hunt as often as required by your Primal Urge is a BTF point. I feel like being on a sacred hunt could stave that off, but failing after too much time had gone by should also ping that point.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T10:13:16-07:00","id":474457,"title":"","content":"Breaking it off or failing might be a breaking point towards the flesh, but it's important to remember that breaking points either way are more of a natural course of existing as a werewolf, not exactly a punishment. At times they're even desirable.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=474428#post474428\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The other thing I remember more clearly is that failing to hunt as often as required by your Primal Urge is a BTF point. I feel like being on a sacred hunt could stave that off, but failing after too much time had gone by should also ping that point.</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, but some hunts are going to take longer. The fiction has a hunt that seems to take course over the period of two years. And our bodhisattva hunters at higher primal urge can't go very long without being on the hunt, but it stands to reason that if they are trying to hunt down concepts and mythical beings like Santa Claus it's likely their hunt is going to take a while without constant, immediate gains.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-09-2015, 01:17 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T10:32:51-07:00","id":474471,"title":"","content":"I agree that someone at Primal Urge 9-10 isn't going to consistently pick hunts that they could finish in 3 days. I was suggesting that if and when they are on a hunt that takes longer than that and they break it off they should be pressed fairly readily into the over-the-limit state, as this would give the prospect of failure more teeth in and of itself.<br /> The book says this:<br /> &quot;[the chart says] how long she can go without being on the Siskur-Dah. If she exceeds that time, she loses a point of Essence each day, and suffers a breaking point towards Flesh.&quot;<br /> <br /> Hmm... in my previous reading of it, it sounded like every day out of bounds was a breaking point towards flesh. I'm less sure that's true now, so it supports my point less well. My point was this, though: While I agree that one isn't always that bad, a lot in quick succession can get bad quickly. You get progressively fewer dice to resist with as you get further along on each scale.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:24:55-07:00","id":474813,"title":"","content":"How about <b><i>pausing</i></b> the Sacred Hunt? Like pack was hunting in the night for the rival pack, but today they only get a trail of enemies and they want to continue at the sunset of the next day. They do not end the Hunt, the only pause it, maybe to go to their day life or jobs. Mine PCs pack totem has Ban that they cannot kill at the day, so this why I ask about it.<br /> <br /> <b>Does this count as ending the Siskur-Dah and as such Breaking Point Toward Flesh? </b>Or merely it's pause in longer Condition and character can return to it next day, as always? <b>Would the Sacred Hunt Rite itself need to be made once more, next sunset?</b> Or does it the Siskur-Dah linger on participants?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:32:21-07:00","id":474850,"title":"","content":"I think a rest would be fine. Sometimes werewolf healing needs some time, but that time doesn't need to be spend idly. Even if your pack can't kill during the day, they can try and follow a trail, do some research, sharpen their weapons, train to defeat their enemies, seek new gifts or old rites. But if they took that next night off, and maybe decided to go on vacation, or a convention in another town, or just take a few nights off, that would probably do it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:34:38-07:00","id":474853,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=474813#post474813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about <b><i>pausing</i></b> the Sacred Hunt? Like pack was hunting in the night for the rival pack, but today they only get a trail of enemies and they want to continue at the sunset of the next day. They do not end the Hunt, the only pause it, maybe to go to their day life or jobs. Mine PCs pack totem has Ban that they cannot kill at the day, so this why I ask about it.<br /> <br /> <b>Does this count as ending the Siskur-Dah and as such Breaking Point Toward Flesh? </b>Or merely it's pause in longer Condition and character can return to it next day, as always? <b>Would the Sacred Hunt Rite itself need to be made once more, next sunset?</b> Or does it the Siskur-Dah linger on participants?</div> </div> </div> </div>Depends on if they take &quot;any significant actions towards ends other than the hunt.&quot; Personally, I wouldn't consider the daily routine to include any &quot;significant actions&quot;. If the time can be fast-forwarded through without missing anything dramatically interesting, it's not significant enough to end the <i>Siskur Dah</i> Condition, in my opinion. That said, if one of the pack members has to do anything noteworthy enough to actually play out, if that thing doesn't involve the hunt, that'll end the hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T13:36:32-07:00","id":474855,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=474813#post474813\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">How about <b><i>pausing</i></b> the Sacred Hunt? Like pack was hunting in the night for the rival pack, but today they only get a trail of enemies and they want to continue at the sunset of the next day. They do not end the Hunt, the only pause it, maybe to go to their day life or jobs. Mine PCs pack totem has Ban that they cannot kill at the day, so this why I ask about it.<br /> <br /> <b>Does this count as ending the Siskur-Dah and as such Breaking Point Toward Flesh? </b>Or merely it's pause in longer Condition and character can return to it next day, as always? <b>Would the Sacred Hunt Rite itself need to be made once more, next sunset?</b> Or does it the Siskur-Dah linger on participants?</div> </div> </div> </div>You can't pause the Sacred Hunt.<br /> <br /> Stop and go off to look after the rest of your life? You've ended the Hunt.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T14:01:26-07:00","id":474889,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Acrozatarim</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=474855#post474855\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You can't pause the Sacred Hunt.<br /> <br /> Stop and go off to look after the rest of your life? You've ended the Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>What if the rest of your life only involves insignificant actions, though?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T14:30:51-07:00","id":474900,"title":"","content":"Waiting it probably part of the hunt; like a stake out or a trap. So going back to base and waiting while doing something connected to the plan (sharpen weapons, work on a fetish, etc.) is allowed. But going home and spending time with the spouse breaks the hunt. I think the intention is that anything that releases tension from the situation probably counts as breaking the hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T14:45:03-07:00","id":474914,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Full Time GM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=474900#post474900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Waiting it probably part of the hunt; like a stake out or a trap. So going back to base and waiting while doing something connected to the plan (sharpen weapons, work on a fetish, etc.) is allowed. But going home and spending time with the spouse breaks the hunt. I think the intention is that anything that releases tension from the situation probably counts as breaking the hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>That makes sense.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T15:29:13-07:00","id":474974,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=474889#post474889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the rest of your life only involves insignificant actions, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Is this a philosophical question? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T16:39:19-07:00","id":475052,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=474889#post474889\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What if the rest of your life only involves insignificant actions, though?</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe you would be one of the special children of Beliar, Maeljin of Sloth.<br /> <br /> Though even they go out and do things, Beliar compounding both the original meaning of the vice <a href=\"http://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Acedia\" target=\"_blank\">acedia</a>, as well as the more modern appreciation of sloth-as-laziness.<br /> <br /> But if you were a werewolf that wasn't even lazy, but still never managed to do nothing but insignificance? That would be so depressing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-09T17:34:17-07:00","id":475097,"title":"","content":"What I meant was, what if, during your time off the hunt, you didn't take any actions that could be described as &quot;significant&quot;?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T02:52:04-07:00","id":475569,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Full Time GM</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=474900#post474900\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Waiting it probably part of the hunt; like a stake out or a trap. So going back to base and waiting while doing something connected to the plan (sharpen weapons, work on a fetish, etc.) is allowed. But going home and spending time with the spouse breaks the hunt. I think the intention is that anything that releases tension from the situation probably counts as breaking the hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> So werewolves need to take a work leave for a couple of days if they make Sacred Hunt on bigger prey? How then Iron Masters live in day to day life? They sustain extensive relationships ( love, work, family ) with humanity as their role of &quot;wolves in sheep clothing&quot;. They disguise would quickly blew off if they would be missing for a few days each month or so...","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T03:07:15-07:00","id":475575,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=475569#post475569\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> So werewolves need to take a work leave for a couple of days if they make Sacred Hunt on bigger prey? How then Iron Masters live in day to day life? They sustain extensive relationships ( love, work, family ) with humanity as their role of &quot;wolves in sheep clothing&quot;. They disguise would quickly blew off if they would be missing for a few days each month or so...</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> They don't have day-to-day lives as we expect them. An Iron Master isn't going to pick a job that requires 9-to-5 soulcrushing monotony, or any job that actively requires their presence. I think it's even stated in the books that the Wolf-Blooded of the Pack are the ones who actually function in normal society because the Werewolves do have the Hunt that's demanding attention.<br /> <br /> Also, where are you seeing the Iron Masters as having extensive relationships with humanity?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/606-aynie","name":"Aynie","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar606_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"223"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T03:20:06-07:00","id":475580,"title":"","content":"Well, they're certainly the ones who generally have the <i>most</i> extensive relationships.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/3166-elfive","name":"Elfive","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar3166_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"8226"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T04:26:07-07:00","id":475604,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=475097#post475097\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">What I meant was, what if, during your time off the hunt, you didn't take any actions that could be described as &quot;significant&quot;?</div> </div> </div> </div>IE you just went and had a sleep to refresh yourself, ate, and let your wounds rest a bit while recovering? You'd probably be fine as long as it's a limited period that you spend doing so.<br /> <br /> 'I go to work at the checkout for a day' is a significant action of non-hunting, unless you're scoping out the people coming through the store because you think your prey will be passing through there and buying something, or whatnot.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T04:59:52-07:00","id":475636,"title":"","content":"Lets keep in mind that at low Primal Urge you aren't required to be on a Siskur-Dah all the time. While it could require you to leave your life behind if you take a momentous hunt, like the one in the fiction, a pack of pups could just hunt on a weekend every month or couple of months. So you can maintain that 9-to-5 of soul crushing drudgery if you want to.<br /> <br /> And even at higher Primal Urge, there's not that great a penalty for breaking off your Siskur-Dah if you want to get back to the Harrison account. Or as Charlaquin pointed out, choosing an insignificant hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":886,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","user":"nofather","date":". 04-10-2015, 08:09 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T06:11:51-07:00","id":475716,"title":"","content":"The minor problem with ending the Hunt is that you need to revoke the Rite each time you return to it - but it only few minutes to one hour, so it can be okay to make this on each night. The larger problem is with Breaking Points Toward Flesh - if you make a bigger Hunt, you will return to it couple nights in a week. Let's say even 5 of them. It's 5 times you go to the Harmony 10 level that we know, is really dangerous, not only to your self, but even to those around you.<br /> <br /> Having those in mind, I would still goes with &quot;pausing&quot; the Siskur-Dah works until you do not make significant action of non-hunting, like have a confrontation in the work or need to perusing the things with your family. Other way it means that Uratha cannot hold any real job or deep personal commitments - yes, it is marked in fiction, but at least I saw as more &quot;werewolves have problems with solving this things&quot; not &quot;we abandon totally our human lives&quot;.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T07:46:11-07:00","id":475815,"title":"","content":"The main thing I am reminded of when reading this is that there are a good handful of places in the book where it talks about Werewolves coming to realize that they can't have normal human lives. The tension created by this issue could really help to underscore that, especially if your characters are trying to pretend that they can.<br /> In the meantime, there are a handful of things they can do to mitigate some of these issues.<br /> <br /> First, they can find different jobs where dissapearing for a couple of days at a time doesn't raise too much suspicion. If their job placement is somehow vital to their overarching mission, then going to that job probably won't conflict with the hunt anyway and this isn't something they have to worry about.<br /> <br /> Second, aim for smaller goals for the overarching hunt. Maybe your Big Hunt is to take out the Bale Hound pack that's messing up the city, but that's the focus of the whole chronicle. In that chronicle, you're going to have stories and chapters. Call hunts on things that can be taken care of more in the short term, such as this group of wound-born spirits or that Hound's influence over city council. Then, once the Bale Hounds are harried and weak and you can take them out directly in one push, call the hunt on them.<br /> <br /> Third, they could plan for the fact that their Harmony is going to struggle. Calling off a hunt regularly is going to play merry hell on their connection to their spirit side, so have them focus on keeping connection to their spirit side. Build really strong connections to their Spiritual Touchstones, and maybe actively avoid their Flesh Touchstones (maybe even fortify this effort with the Anchored Merit). Have someone learn the Totemic Empowerment Rite and make liberal use of it. The pack as a whole can only use it once per day, but it's always a breaking point towards spirit.<br /> <br /> I see a lot of potential for character development and role playing in this, but it's a thing you might want to give your players fair warning about. Well, maybe you'll wait til they hit Harmony 8 and then make them roll Wits + Intelligence before giving them fair warning <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/wink.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Wink\" smilieid=\"4\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> &quot;Roll Wits + Intelligence&quot;<br /> &quot;Success!&quot;<br /> &quot;You realize that the pressures of keeping up your day job and continuously dropping and picking up the hunt are going to quickly strain your relationship to your spiritual half. You're going to need to find ways to focus on your spirit connection...&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T08:00:00-07:00","id":475835,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=475716#post475716\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The minor problem with ending the Hunt is that you need to revoke the Rite each time you return to it - but it only few minutes to one hour, so it can be okay to make this on each night. The larger problem is with Breaking Points Toward Flesh - if you make a bigger Hunt, you will return to it couple nights in a week. Let's say even 5 of them. It's 5 times you go to the Harmony 10 level that we know, is really dangerous, not only to your self, but even to those around you.<br /> <br /> Having those in mind, I would still goes with &quot;pausing&quot; the Siskur-Dah works until you do not make significant action of non-hunting, like have a confrontation in the work or need to perusing the things with your family. Other way it means that Uratha cannot hold any real job or deep personal commitments - yes, it is marked in fiction, but at least I saw as more &quot;werewolves have problems with solving this things&quot; not &quot;we abandon totally our human lives&quot;.</div> </div> </div> </div>The pack should either commit to the longer hunt entirely, or call several, shorter-term hunts to hit individual objectives in their overall plan for the foe.<br /> <br /> Returning to a hunt a couple of nights a week and spending the rest of the week living a normal human life with no direct relevance to the hunt in question is <i>absolutely</i> taking significant action towards ends other than the hunt, and will break it off with the commensurate effects.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T08:57:35-07:00","id":475905,"title":"","content":"My one big question about whether doing other things would break off the hunt is this:<br /> <br /> When hunting, not everyone is active all the time. Perhaps one or two people in a group are going on ahead to flush out the prey while the others wait. Sometimes you just need to wait for your prey to get into the appropriate position.<br /> <br /> So in Ham's situation where people are going to work, what if the situation is such that some of them go to work with the intention of being ready when the time comes. Their mind and focus are on then hunt, but they are physically present and active in a place seemingly not directly related. Before the moment comes when they fail to spring into action because they were distracted at the wrong moment by their work, have they broken off the hunt?<br /> <br /> Edit: in this suggested scenario, at least one or two packmates are on more active surveillance or something and each person at work either has a specified time of action or is awaiting a call.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":4563,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","user":"TerraBen","date":". 04-10-2015, 11:59 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T09:32:35-07:00","id":475935,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=475905#post475905\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">My one big question about whether doing other things would break off the hunt is this:<br /> <br /> When hunting, not everyone is active all the time. Perhaps one or two people in a group are going on ahead to flush out the prey while the others wait. Sometimes you just need to wait for your prey to get into the appropriate position.<br /> <br /> So in Ham's situation where people are going to work, what if the situation is such that some of them go to work with the intention of being ready when the time comes. Their mind and focus are on then hunt, but they are physically present and active in a place seemingly not directly related. Before the moment comes when they fail to spring into action because they were distracted at the wrong moment by their work, have they broken off the hunt?<br /> <br /> Edit: in this suggested scenario, at least one or two packmates are on more active surveillance or something and each person at work either has a specified time of action or is awaiting a call.</div> </div> </div> </div>Generally I'd say that would break the hunter. But I could see that being an interesting scene that might be worth an exception if there is an interesting story (and probably suffers a complication) as a result.<br /> <br /> &quot;You go into the gas station, late at night, and find the attendant pacing behind the counter, phone in hand. You wait, gas money in hand, for thirty second before clearing your throat loudly. You jump back when the man <i>snarls</i> at you, fixing you with bloodshot eyes. Suddenly you decide you don't need change, put the money on the counter, and quickly step back outside. As you fill up you see him through the window, pacing with phone in hand except when he pauses to look out the windows into the tall grass across the highway.&quot;","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/785-full-time-gm","name":"Full Time GM","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar785_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"174"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T09:45:16-07:00","id":475945,"title":"","content":"The Siskur-Dah Condition applies to each packmate individually, not to the pack as a whole. So each character who went back to work would Resolve the Condition on themselves, and each character who remained vigilant would keep the Condition.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T10:04:11-07:00","id":475976,"title":"","content":"That seems to me like a case of mechanics interfering with narrative. <br /> In the case where the prey is holed up and there's nothing for it but waiting, having the whole pack stake it out (intead of just the Irakka) would be counterproductive. Everyone else needs to go somewhere else and do something else while they await the appropriate time.<br /> In the case where the next step of the hunt is to secure the favor of some powerful spirit/senator, you don't want the whole pack going to the meeting, just the Ithaeur/Elodoth and a one-man-back-up. Everyone else needs to go somewhere else and do something else.<br /> <br /> I guess in these circumstances we go back to the &quot;more short-term hunts&quot; rule of thumb. Well, the second one, maybe. In the first example, once it's go time, you might not have the 3-6 minutes to spare to redo the Siskur-Dah Rite and get everyone back on The Hunt.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T10:16:28-07:00","id":475998,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=475976#post475976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That seems to me like a case of mechanics interfering with narrative.</div> </div> </div> </div>I don't think it is. This way, if some of the pack members give up on the hunt, while others are still determined to see it through, the quitters don't ruin it for the ones who want to finish what they started.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=475976#post475976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">In the case where the prey is holed up and there's nothing for it but waiting, having the whole pack stake it out (intead of just the Irakka) would be counterproductive. Everyone else needs to go somewhere else and do something else while they await the appropriate time.<br /> In the case where the next step of the hunt is to secure the favor of some powerful spirit/senator, you don't want the whole pack going to the meeting, just the Ithaeur/Elodoth and a one-man-back-up. Everyone else needs to go somewhere else and do something else.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure, but they can still do things that will help the hunt in the mean time. Do some party buffing rituals, prepare the weapons, set a trap, or even just rest and recover your strength. If you've got downtime while other members of your pack are taking care of a crucial part of the hunt that requires a small group, and you chose to spend that time organizing your stamp collection instead of helping support the effort in other ways, you blew it. You're off the hunt. Come back when you're ready to commit.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=475976#post475976\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I guess in these circumstances we go back to the &amp;quot;more short-term hunts&amp;quot; rule of thumb. Well, the second one, maybe. In the first example, once it's go time, you might not have the 3-6 minutes to spare to redo the Siskur-Dah Rite and get everyone back on The Hunt.</div> </div> </div> </div>Or just short-term goals that are part of the larger hunt. That wouldn't break the Condition, so you don't need to set aside time to renew the ritual.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T10:28:02-07:00","id":476015,"title":"","content":"It seems to fit with everything else. If you go all out and decide to live the life of endless hunt, you're going to lean more towards the spirit side. If you're going try and maintain a more normal life, you're going to lean more towards your flesh side. A more balanced werewolf could embrace their flesh side by having a non-traditional job, such as a travel writer or photographer, missionary or doctor without borders, something that allows them to hunt as much as they can when they need to. I guess a truly balanced werewolf or one more bent towards the flesh might actually get a career that allows them to pursue great hunts as their job. International assassins, bounty hunters, law enforcement agencies, explorers or scientists.<br /> <br /> I don't find anything wrong with the idea that the alpha of a pack may be gung ho for the hunt and other members of their pack might not want to. It leads to choices for the character. How does the alpha deal with it? They could be a 'weekend hunter' with their pack every once and awhile but when they want to they can hunt alone, you only need one person to perform a Siskur-Dah. Or maybe they try to get the pack more into the hunt. Maybe they decide it's time for them to find a pack with similar desires. It opens up more options.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T10:50:49-07:00","id":476066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=475998#post475998\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Sure, but they can still do things that will help the hunt in the mean time. Do some party buffing rituals, prepare the weapons, set a trap, or even just rest and recover your strength. If you've got downtime while other members of your pack are taking care of a crucial part of the hunt that requires a small group, and you chose to spend that time organizing your stamp collection instead of helping support the effort in other ways, you blew it. You're off the hunt. Come back when you're ready to commit.</div> </div> </div> </div>I like this. This helps. To play devil's advocate a little, though, lets run with this holed-up scenario a little bit. You're tracking your quarry down. You as a group find that he's in an incredibly fortified location and nobody knows any of the gifts for luring someone out. You take a moment to asign roles for the time being: Irakka takes first watch of shadowing the building in case he comes out, Ithaeur HiD goes off to find a Nature spirit that can teach him a Luring gift, Rahu and Elodoth go home to rest up. Two days later, the prey hasn't come out and the Ithaeur still hasn't been granted the Gift yet. Are the people not on the watch supposed to just sit and meditate while there's nothing for them to do? If the stamp collection happens to be around and they pick it up, are they off the hunt?<br /> <br /> Edit: I guess one option would be to take advantage of the new extended action rules that let you almost finish and thing and come back to it later. Then they can drop the one hunt, start starting up the next one, but put the last roll on hold until they get the call. Finishing the ritual wouldn't take but a few seconds at that point, and then the hunt is on.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/4563-terraben","name":"TerraBen","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"278"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-10T10:59:52-07:00","id":476094,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>TerraBen</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=476066#post476066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I like this. This helps. To play devil's advocate a little, though, lets run with this holed-up scenario a little bit. You're tracking your quarry down. You as a group find that he's in an incredibly fortified location and nobody knows any of the gifts for luring someone out. You take a moment to asign roles for the time being: Irakka takes first watch of shadowing the building in case he comes out, Ithaeur HiD goes off to find a Nature spirit that can teach him a Luring gift, Rahu and Elodoth go home to rest up. Two days later, the prey hasn't come out and the Ithaeur still hasn't been granted the Gift yet. Are the people not on the watch supposed to just sit and meditate while there's nothing for them to do? If the stamp collection happens to be around and they pick it up, are they off the hunt?<br /> <br /> Edit: I guess one option would be to take advantage of the new extended action rules that let you almost finish and thing and come back to it later. Then they can drop the one hunt, start starting up the next one, but put the last roll on hold until they get the call. Finishing the ritual wouldn't take but a few seconds at that point, and then the hunt is on.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm not really sure why the Rahu and the Elodoth in this situation don't help the Ithaur track down a nature spirit, or rotate watch with the Irraka. Or look for a weakness in the prey's fortress, maybe they can find a way in. Or try to smoke the prey out. Or cut off their supply line and wait them out. Or build some seige weapons. If you can't think of anything you can do to help, you're not thinking creatively enough. And you know, sometimes the best way you can help your pack is just to eat the Breaking Point and get out of their hair for a little while. Especially in a situation like this, they can always send you a spirit messenger when it's time to make your move and you can renew the Sacred Hunt rite on yourself.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T13:25:50-07:00","id":480648,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charlaquin</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=475945#post475945\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Siskur-Dah Condition applies to each packmate individually, not to the pack as a whole. So each character who went back to work would Resolve the Condition on themselves, and each character who remained vigilant would keep the Condition.</div> </div> </div> </div>The Resolution for the Condition reads (emphasis mine): <br /> <br /> &quot;The prey is brought down (a kill is not<br /> necessary) or the <b>pack</b> breaks off the Siskur-Dah by taking any<br /> significant actions towards ends other than the hunt.&quot;<br /> <br /> You are in this as a pack, not individually.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><b>Eric Christian Berg</b><br /> <i>Onyx Path Freelancer</i><br /> Promethean: The Created Second Edition, Dark Eras Companion","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2019-eberg","name":"eberg","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar2019_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jan 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"284"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T14:29:27-07:00","id":480712,"title":"","content":"I suppose it could be read that way. I don't care for that interpretation because it prevents committed Packmates from continuing the hunt if the majority decide to give up.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Going by Willow now, or Wil for short. She/Her/Hers.","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/269-charlaquin","name":"Charlaquin","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar269_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"10831"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T14:38:07-07:00","id":480734,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>eberg</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=480648#post480648\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">You are in this as a pack, not individually.</div> </div> </div> </div>I think I really like that interpretation, since it allows the largest number of situations to make narrative sense. The storyteller just has to make a personal call: Is the Blood Talon working the gas station itching and eager to return to the hunt the moment his shift is over? He's still got Siskur-Dah. Is the Iron Master more interested in sending machine spirits to troll people on the internet? He's off the Siskur-Dah.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1505-charles-red","name":"Charles Red","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1505_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"84"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T14:53:46-07:00","id":480747,"title":"","content":"Plus lets keep in mind you can call the rite on a few packmates without involving the entire pack. If it gets called off because the Iron Slacker you can even probably call a Siskur-Dah just for yourself.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-04-14T22:43:31-07:00","id":481123,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Charles Red</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=480734#post480734\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I think I really like that interpretation, since it allows the largest number of situations to make narrative sense. The storyteller just has to make a personal call: Is the Blood Talon working the gas station itching and eager to return to the hunt the moment his shift is over? He's still got Siskur-Dah. Is the Iron Master more interested in sending machine spirits to troll people on the internet? He's off the Siskur-Dah.</div> </div> </div> </div>I now have the image of a pack of Forsaken having a Siskur-Dah based on pranks. Stealing an Arisen's Relic and blowing raspberries at it in the Shadow. Hunting down Unchained for the purpose of messing with them until they have the blow their cover by Going Loud. Convincing the nearby Crone Cult to worship a Lune and laugh as it makes them go batshit insane. <br /> <br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/604-shock","name":"Shock","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar604_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1071"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T14:45:03-08:00","id":1050081,"title":"","content":"I suspect someone must've bullied Wyrd pretty harshly for not taking Sacred Hunt once.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T14:50:32-08:00","id":1050087,"title":"","content":"He hasn't explained, but in the game he's running it sounds like only one person had it, and they are 'out of commission,' leaving the pack without their sacred hunt provider.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T14:55:28-08:00","id":1050093,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=1050087#post1050087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He hasn't explained, but in the game he's running it sounds like only one person had it, and they are 'out of commission,' leaving the pack without their sacred hunt provider.</div> </div> </div> </div>NPC the guy for the 10 minutes it takes to pull the rite off? Most of the time we don't even roll it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T23:22:30-08:00","id":1050339,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=1050087#post1050087\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">He hasn't explained, but in the game he's running it sounds like only one person had it, and they are 'out of commission,' leaving the pack without their sacred hunt provider.</div> </div> </div> </div>My PCs pack had one Sacred Hunt ritemaster - he got in one fight pretty badly. What's important - PCs were only Forsaken Uratha in nearby. Once invoking Sacred Hunt and then do not being able - well, it was a hit for starting Uratha I run.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-16T23:31:43-08:00","id":1050340,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=1050339#post1050339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My PCs pack had one Sacred Hunt ritemaster - he got in one fight pretty badly. What's important - PCs were only Forsaken Uratha in nearby. Once invoking Sacred Hunt and then do not being able - well, it was a hit for starting Uratha I run.</div> </div> </div> </div>Uratha can learn rites from other werewolves or spirits (p. 139). Unless no one in your pack can even try and bargain with spirits to teach someone else the rite, being the only Forsaken in an area means little.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><i>Writer. Developer.</i> <b>World of Darkness</b> | <b>Chronicles of Darkness</b> | <b>The Trinity Continuum</b>","edited":{"userid":156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","user":"Bunyip","date":". 02-17-2017, 02:39 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/156-bunyip","name":"Bunyip","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1880"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T19:06:37-08:00","id":1050844,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=1050339#post1050339\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> My PCs pack had one Sacred Hunt ritemaster - he got in one fight pretty badly. What's important - PCs were only Forsaken Uratha in nearby. Once invoking Sacred Hunt and then do not being able - well, it was a hit for starting Uratha I run.</div> </div> </div> </div>They don't even have a totem to teach it to them? If they do, it's been on sacred hunts before. Can teach it.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T20:59:37-08:00","id":1050871,"title":"","content":"Wait - spirits can teach Rites OUTSIDE their concept?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T21:40:50-08:00","id":1050885,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>wyrdhamster</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=1050871#post1050871\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Wait - spirits can teach Rites OUTSIDE their concept?</div> </div> </div> </div>They probably still can't, but the concept of predation is fairly prevalent in the Shadow, and the concept of the hunt is just one step away from predation.<br /> <br /> That, and the pack finding a &quot;hidden master&quot; to teach them, like in wuxia works, is a nice touch to any story. The hidden master in question being inhuman only adds to the fun.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-17T23:45:48-08:00","id":1050899,"title":"","content":"Gifts rely on the spirits concept. A spirit can learn a rite simply due to age or knowing werewolves. Rites are ancient pacts made by werewolves or werewolf-kind to age old spirits. It's like you don't have to be a geographer to tell people Australia exists.<br /> <br /> That said, the way a spirit is likely to know about the rite is going to be tainted by their concept, and would probably show in how the rite is conducted.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T04:45:09-08:00","id":1050947,"title":"","content":"Oh right, it was Gifts, not Rites, like nofather said.<br /> <br /> Hmm... that gives me a thought. I do wonder how spirit-taught werewolves will conduct the Siskur-Dah, compared to kin-taught werewolves.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T05:23:55-08:00","id":1050962,"title":"","content":"hi guys, need some clarifications about hunting spirits: when you are hunting them, you can both destroy them, gathering whole essence, or chasing down them, learning the spirit's gift.. mechanically, how does this last thing work?? i mean, you trak the spirit down, you find him and then?? the werevolf has to fight him?? speak him?? convince him??<br /> <br /> and last thing: how many ways do you have to fight a ephemeral entity?? the gift of death gives you the chance to attack ghosts with your natural weapon, not spirits. So without the right bane ( or be 2 ranks above them), how could you fight them?? because, in the hisil, you can damage them, but not in the flesh ( manifested or not, you can t hurt them)<br /> <br /> thx for answers","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T05:43:48-08:00","id":1050970,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=1050962#post1050962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hi guys, need some clarifications about hunting spirits: when you are hunting them, you can both destroy them, gathering whole essence, or chasing down them, learning the spirit's gift.. mechanically, how does this last thing work?? i mean, you trak the spirit down, you find him and then?? the werevolf has to fight him?? speak him?? convince him??</div> </div> </div> </div>By the time the pack has hunted down the spirit, it should be subjugated and will surrender rather than fighting to the death. Then the werewolves can just &quot;nicely ask&quot; the spirit to teach a Gift/Rite. The spirit will comply because, well, if it would die rather than aid the werewolves then it wouldn't have surrendered in the first place, and the werewolves can just insta-kill the spirit that it is now under their mercy as the Siskur-Dah dictates.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> and last thing: how many ways do you have to fight a ephemeral entity?? the gift of death gives you the chance to attack ghosts with your natural weapon, not spirits. So without the right bane ( or be 2 ranks above them), how could you fight them?? because, in the hisil, you can damage them, but not in the flesh ( manifested or not, you can t hurt them)<br /> <br /> thx for answers </div> </div> </div>Therefore, researching a spirit's bane and ban is of utmost importance when fighting it. The bane to hurt it in the Flesh, and the ban to force it away from its Essence sources so that it falls dormant or flees into the Shadow.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>MtAw Homebrew:<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1051456-even-more-legacies-updated-to-2e#post1051456\" target=\"_blank\">Even more Legacies, updated to 2E</a><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/mage-the-awakening/1443819-new-2e-legacies-expanded\" target=\"_blank\">New 2E Legacies, expanded</a>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12619-21c-hermit","name":"21C Hermit","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12619_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3489"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T05:55:08-08:00","id":1050974,"title":"","content":"really thanks.. had some strunggling on understand some mechanics ( sometimes they are quite obscure, like the influence by the gift)<br /> <br /> anyway, i remember somethings about the spirits that can be wounded even in twilight.. but can t find this rule ( a gift?? an hunter 's aspect??), but of course, the first stuff i had thought was the bane.. but in the hisil for example, you can damage them is it right?? but knowing the right ban helps you to chose right method to make them flee from their influence area, for example.. is this right??<br /> so, with resonance shaper, we could change the resonance according to the spirit's ban to weak him and convince to collaborate with me<br /> am i right?? <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> thank you","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T09:13:29-08:00","id":1051018,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=1050962#post1050962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">and last thing: how many ways do you have to fight a ephemeral entity?? the gift of death gives you the chance to attack ghosts with your natural weapon, not spirits. So without the right bane ( or be 2 ranks above them), how could you fight them?? because, in the hisil, you can damage them, but not in the flesh ( manifested or not, you can t hurt them)</div> </div> </div> </div>If an ephemeral entity is manifested in the gurihal, the world of flesh, they're either in Twilight or in some other physical form. If they're in another physical form, they can be hurt by a simple punch. The only trick is when they're in Twilight, in which case you need to use a bane, the sacred hunt of the Ithaeur, a fetish like the Whisper Knife, the Twilight Purge rite, the Banish rite, the totem of the pack who can also go into Twilight, Barghest gift facet if it's a death-infused spirit, you could even use Shadowbind, Bottle Spirit or Fetish rites to either bind it or scare it back across the Gauntlet. Or you could do a simple mundane 'getting rid of the Conditions that allow it to linger in Twilight.' Resonance Shaper could be good for that if it's using a locus to stay.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T10:26:41-08:00","id":1051051,"title":"","content":"thank you.. now it s way more clear..<br /> so, if they are not in piysical form you can jsut hurt them with bane or overranking them ( or with just of one rite/tricks you described)<br /> there are rules spread everywhere.. is not easy to see them clearly<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12670-dante90","name":"Dante90","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"42"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T12:39:03-08:00","id":1051105,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=1051051#post1051051\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">thank you.. now it s way more clear..<br /> so, if they are not in piysical form you can jsut hurt them with bane or overranking them ( or with just of one rite/tricks you described)<br /> there are rules spread everywhere.. is not easy to see them clearly</div> </div> </div> </div>It's no problem. The big thing in storyteller is that, basically, for every rule there's an exception. Nothing's really hard set, so you can fiddle with it as you like.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T12:56:44-08:00","id":1051111,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Dante90</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=1050962#post1050962\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">hi guys, need some clarifications about hunting spirits: when you are hunting them, you can both destroy them, gathering whole essence, or chasing down them, learning the spirit's gift.. mechanically, how does this last thing work?? i mean, you trak the spirit down, you find him and then?? the werevolf has to fight him?? speak him?? convince him??<br /> <br /> and last thing: how many ways do you have to fight a ephemeral entity?? the gift of death gives you the chance to attack ghosts with your natural weapon, not spirits. So without the right bane ( or be 2 ranks above them), how could you fight them?? because, in the hisil, you can damage them, but not in the flesh ( manifested or not, you can t hurt them)<br /> <br /> thx for answers</div> </div> </div> </div>Yes, you usually strong arm them. &quot;I'll eat you unless you teach me how to handle fire without it burning me anymore&quot; works pretty well. Other more esoteric packs challenge spirits in other ways. A spirit of shadow &amp; secrets that can discorporate at will when the going gets tough likely won't be worried about mere physical threats, but blackmailing it with information being spread about how it trucked with the neighboring spirit lord against the one which he currently owes fealty would work better.<br /> <br /> Or amusing a spirit of enigmas into teaching you how to read people like open books (Know Thy Prey) with a competition of riddles. They're called Gifts after all.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2017-02-18T12:59:05-08:00","id":1051113,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>nofather</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/433128-siskur-dah-2ed-sacred-hunt-and-it-s-secrets?p=1051018#post1051018\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> If an ephemeral entity is manifested in the gurihal, the world of flesh, they're either in Twilight or in some other physical form. If they're in another physical form, they can be hurt by a simple punch. The only trick is when they're in Twilight, in which case you need to use a bane, the sacred hunt of the <b>Bone Shadow</b>, a fetish like the Whisper Knife, the Twilight Purge rite, the Banish rite, the totem of the pack who can also go into Twilight, Barghest gift facet if it's a death-infused spirit, you could even use Shadowbind, Bottle Spirit or Fetish rites to either bind it or scare it back across the Gauntlet. Or you could do a simple mundane 'getting rid of the Conditions that allow it to linger in Twilight.' Resonance Shaper could be good for that if it's using a locus to stay.</div> </div> </div> </div>Emphasis mine.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/12191-malus","name":"Malus","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar12191_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1562"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}